# Trusted Domains - Standard Mode
# Core software development domains only
# Version: 1.1.0
# Last Updated: 2025-12-16
#
# Selection criteria:
# - Official documentation sites
# - Major code hosting platforms
# - Essential package registries
# - Trusted Q&A communities
#
# ============================================================
# BEST PRACTICES FOR ADDING DOMAINS
# ============================================================
# 1. Use BASE DOMAINS for subdomain coverage:
#    ✓ anthropic.com     → allows docs.anthropic.com, api.anthropic.com, etc.
#    ✗ www.anthropic.com → only allows www, NOT other subdomains
#
# 2. Use SPECIFIC SUBDOMAINS for limited access:
#    ✓ developer.mozilla.org → only MDN, not all of mozilla.org
#    ✓ docs.python.org       → only docs, not all of python.org
#
# 3. NEVER include paths (they don't work):
#    ✗ aws.amazon.com/blogs  → Invalid! Use: aws.amazon.com
#
# 4. See README.md for full documentation
# ============================================================
#
# Format: One domain per line (comments start with #)
# Note: Base domains auto-match all subdomains (e.g., anthropic.com matches console.anthropic.com)

# Anthropic / Claude (base domains - auto-matches all subdomains)
# Covers: console, api, docs, support, trust, status, privacy, www, etc.
anthropic.com
claude.ai
claude.com

# Documentation
developer.mozilla.org

# Code Hosting
github.com
raw.githubusercontent.com

# Package Registries
npmjs.com
pypi.org

# Q&A / Community
stackoverflow.com
